    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d866">

                <pb facs="0791" n="619" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg619"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 703.5263/3</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Willard</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-04-11T10:00:00+00:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 11, 1917, 10 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 6.30 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>469. Department’s 396, April 9, 4 p.m. Instructions have been given and Spanish
                    Embassy, Vienna, has actually taken charge American interests Austria-Hungary.
                    Similar instructions sent by Foreign Office in regard to British and Japanese
                    interests.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Willard</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
